---
import LogoMark from '../../../brand/logo-mark.svg'
import Logo from '../../../brand/logo.svg'
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'

const downloads = [
  { href: '/brand/logo.svg', label: 'Lockup', format: 'SVG', note: 'EV blue mark, text in currentColor' },
  { href: '/brand/logo-mark.svg', label: 'Mark', format: 'SVG', note: 'EV blue, square' },
  { href: '/brand/logo-on-light.png', label: 'Lockup for light backgrounds', format: 'PNG', note: '1600 px, transparent' },
  { href: '/brand/logo-on-dark.png', label: 'Lockup for dark backgrounds', format: 'PNG', note: '1600 px, transparent' },
]

const rules = [
  ['Clear space', 'Keep free space around the logo at least as large as the plug in the mark.'],
  ['Minimum size', 'Mark 16 px, lockup 120 px wide.'],
  [
    'Colour',
    'The mark is EV blue #2563eb, the word "evicons" takes the text colour around it (currentColor) and ".dev" the same colour at 65 % opacity. On a single-colour background where blue does not work, the whole logo may be one colour. Do not use other colours.',
  ],
  ['Do not distort', 'Scale it only proportionally. Do not stretch, slant, rotate or rearrange the mark and the wordmark.'],
  ['No effects', 'No shadows, outlines, gradients or glows.'],
]

const colours = [
  { name: 'EV blue', hex: '#2563eb', use: 'Accent' },
  { name: 'Available', hex: '#16a34a', use: 'Status' },
  { name: 'Occupied', hex: '#d97706', use: 'Status' },
  { name: 'Faulted', hex: '#dc2626', use: 'Status' },
  { name: 'Out of service', hex: '#71717a', use: 'Status' },
  { name: 'Unknown', hex: '#0891b2', use: 'Status' },
  { name: 'Reserved', hex: '#7c3aed', use: 'Status' },
  { name: 'Queue', hex: '#c2410c', use: 'Status' },
]

const panel = 'flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-border'
const light = 'bg-white text-zinc-900'
// zinc-900, one step lighter than the dark page (#09090b), so the sample reads as its own panel.
const dark = 'bg-zinc-900 text-zinc-100'
---

<Base title="Brand – EVicons" description="The EVicons logo, how to use it, and the colours of the project.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-3xl">Brand</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-muted">
      The EVicons mark is a lowercase e drawn as a charging cable that ends in a plug. The mark is EV blue; the
      wordmark takes the text colour around it (<code class="font-mono text-sm">currentColor</code>), so the same
      file works on light and dark backgrounds.
    </p>

    <section aria-labelledby="logo" class="mt-12">
      <h2 id="logo" class="text-2xl">Logo</h2>
      <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 md:grid-cols-[2fr_1fr]">
        <div class:list={[panel, light, 'col-span-2 px-6 py-10 sm:py-14 md:col-span-1']}>
          <Logo class="h-auto w-full max-w-[22rem]" role="img" aria-label="EVicons logo on a light background" />
        </div>
        <div class:list={[panel, light, 'order-3 py-10 sm:py-14 md:order-none']}>
          <LogoMark width={96} height={96} role="img" aria-label="EVicons mark on a light background" />
        </div>
        <div class:list={[panel, dark, 'col-span-2 px-6 py-10 sm:py-14 md:col-span-1']}>
          <Logo class="h-auto w-full max-w-[22rem]" role="img" aria-label="EVicons logo on a dark background" />
        </div>
        <div class:list={[panel, dark, 'order-4 py-10 sm:py-14 md:order-none']}>
          <LogoMark width={96} height={96} role="img" aria-label="EVicons mark on a dark background" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="downloads" class="mt-12">
      <h2 id="downloads" class="text-2xl">Downloads</h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {
          downloads.map((d) => (
            <li>
              <a
                href={d.href}
                download
                class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 rounded-lg border border-border px-4 py-3 no-underline hover:bg-surface"
              >
                <span>
                  <span class="block font-medium text-fg">{d.label}</span>
                  <span class="block text-sm text-muted">{d.note}</span>
                </span>
                <span class="rounded border border-border px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-link">{d.format}</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">
        Sources and rules are also in <a href="https://github.com/evicons/evicons/tree/main/brand">brand/</a> on GitHub.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="rules" class="mt-12">
      <h2 id="rules" class="text-2xl">Rules</h2>
      <dl class="mt-6 grid max-w-3xl gap-4">
        {
          rules.map(([term, text]) => (
            <div class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[10rem_1fr] sm:gap-6">
              <dt class="font-medium">{term}</dt>
              <dd class="text-muted">{text}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="colours" class="mt-12">
      <h2 id="colours" class="text-2xl">Colours</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-muted">
        EV blue is the accent of the project. The status colours are suggestions for apps; the icons themselves contain
        no colour.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-4">
        {
          colours.map((c) => (
            <li class="overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-border">
              <div class="h-16" style={`background:${c.hex}`} />
              <div class="px-3 py-2">
                <span class="block font-medium">{c.name}</span>
                <span class="block font-mono text-sm text-muted">
                  {c.hex} · {c.use}
                </span>
              </div>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="name" class="mt-12">
      <h2 id="name" class="text-2xl">Name</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-muted">
        Write the name as <strong class="font-semibold text-fg">EVicons</strong>: capital E and V, lowercase “icons”, one
        word. Not “EV Icons”, “EV-icons”, “Evicons” or “evicons”; the lowercase form is only used in the logo, the domain
        evicons.dev and the npm scope <code class="font-mono text-sm">@evicons</code>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
